.TH LAYA 1 "@DATE@" "Oh My Laya @VERSION@"
.SH NAME
laya \- native local AI decisions, routing, and learning
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B laya
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Oh My Laya provides a local decision workbench and an MCP bridge for agent hosts.
Help, version, completion and manual generation do not start services or load models.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B dashboard [--port PORT] [--no-open]
Start the service if needed and open the workbench. Default port is 18686.
Port 0 selects a temporary port. --no-open prints a private pairing URL instead.
.TP
.B status
Print JSON service, recording, usage reconciliation and resource status without starting it.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the running service. Stored records are preserved.
.TP
.B snake [demo-options]
Run the installed offline demo with local weights. Alias: --snake.
Stops an idle service; refuses when inference is busy. Demo arguments are forwarded unchanged.
.TP
.B mcp
Run the MCP stdio bridge. Intended for agent hosts. Starts the local service on demand.
.TP
.B service [--port PORT]
Run the local service in the foreground.
.TP
.B version
Print version, release date and repository. Alias: --version. Development builds use -dev.
.TP
.B help [command]
Show general or command help. Aliases: --help and command --help.
.TP
.B completion bash|zsh|fish
Print shell completion. No runtime dependencies or service required.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
laya dashboard
laya dashboard --port 18686 --no-open
laya status
laya help dashboard
laya version
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LAYA_PORT
Default local HTTP port.
.TP
.B LAYA_WORKBENCH_DIR
Workbench data directory. Defaults to ~/.local/share/oh-my-laya/workbench.
.TP
.B LAYA_PYTHON
Installed Python interpreter used for local inference and native usage reconciliation.
.TP
.B LAYA_NATIVE_USAGE_SYNC
Set to 1 by the installer to enable periodic native Codex usage reconciliation.
Recording and replay consent must also be enabled. No model is loaded for reconciliation.
.SH FILES
~/.local/share/oh-my-laya/workbench/laya.sqlite3 stores local decisions and feedback.
Native usage reconciliation reads local Codex metadata and writes numeric feedback only
for verifiably matched recorded decisions. Estimates are hypothetical, not measured savings.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; nonzero on invalid input or an operation failure.
.SH CAVEATS
Inference and the demo require the installed Python runtime and local weights.
Collection is never enabled by a help or dashboard command.
Keep pairing URLs private. Completion activation depends on your shell configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR zsh (1),
.BR fish (1)
.PP
https://github.com/leo1394/oh-my-laya
